{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27088987","formula":"C₆H₈N₂O₂","hill":"C6H8N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":8.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"THPO"},"descriptions":{"en":"THPO, also known as 4,5,6,7-tetrahydroisoxazolo[4,5-c]pyridin-3(2H)-one, is a relatively weak GABA reuptake inhibitor with some glial selectivity. It is a synthetic and conformationally restrained analogue of the GABAA receptor agonist and weak GABA reuptake inhibitor muscimol (found in Amanita muscaria). Unlike muscimol however, THPO is a selective GABA reuptake inhibitor and lacks GABAA receptor affinity."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":1695,"mass":140.14,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CNCC2=C1ONC2=O","inchikey":"SXXLKZCNJHJYFL-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4,5,6,7-tetrahydro-[1,2]oxazolo[4,5-c]pyridin-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1695","atoms":18,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.937,"y":-1.732,"z":-0.065,"el":"O"},{"x":2.319,"y":1.473,"z":0.065,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.156,"y":1.067,"z":-0.33,"el":"N"},{"x":2.047,"y":-0.853,"z":-0.028,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.527,"y":-1.342,"z":-0.044,"el":"C"},{"x":0.178,"y":0.44,"z":0.028,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.501,"y":-0.203,"z":0.329,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.122,"y":-0.853,"z":-0.032,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.81,"y":1.538,"z":0.05,"el":"C"},{"x":1.635,"y":0.465,"z":0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.764,"y":-1.719,"z":-1.046,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.651,"y":-2.17,"z":0.662,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.516,"y":-0.494,"z":0.038,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.512,"y":-0.061,"z":1.418,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.844,"y":1.981,"z":1.052,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.513,"y":2.326,"z":-0.651,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.842,"y":1.778,"z":-0.079,"el":"H"},{"x":2.984,"y":-1.234,"z":-0.046,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,7,1],[1,9,2],[2,6,1],[2,8,1],[2,16,1],[3,9,1],[3,17,1],[4,6,1],[4,7,1],[4,10,1],[4,11,1],[5,7,2],[5,8,1],[5,9,1],[6,12,1],